  "live_records": {
    "q-39181": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39181",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Determine whether $v=[\\begin{aligned}-4+7\\text{i} \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 13 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?",
      "worked_solution": "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 13 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4+7\\text{i} \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-49-28\\text{i} \\\\ 91\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}49{\\text{i}}^{2}-28\\text{i} \\\\ 91\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =7\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}-4+7\\text{i} \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =7\\text{i}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=7\\text{i}v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =7\\text{i}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
